<title>CANADA: Canada's west Prairies to see rain, sun in east.</title>
<headline>Canada's west Prairies to see rain, sun in east.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canada's Prairies were forecast on Thursday to see rain in the west and sun in the east, Environment Canada said.</p>
<p>Alberta should see a few showers in the south and central regions with highs of +4 to +8 Celsius.</p>
<p>Saskatchewan should see showers in the south and highs of +4 to +8 Celsius.</p>
<p>Manitoba should see mainly sunny skies with highs of +5 to +9 Celsius.</p>
<p>Average day time highs at this time of year is +3 Celsius.</p>
<p>((--Gilbert Le Gras 204 947 3548))</p>
